 "captions": {
  "script": "These mountains look like a glitch in the game. But nobody painted them. Glitch Diary, entry twelve. The Rainbow Mountains of Zhangye, in northwest China. Red, yellow, even green stripes run across the hills. Each stripe was once a layer of sand and mud, laid flat over millions of years. Iron oxide made the red. Other minerals made the yellow and green. But that's not the strange part. These layers were born flat. Now they stand tilted, like books knocked over. And scientists still can't agree on one thing... Most say India crashed into Asia fifty million years ago, and folded the rock. New research says some folding is even older. Then wind and rain stripped the hills bare. Would you believe this is real? Tell me in the comments. Follow for the next entry of my glitch diary. Because these mountains only look painted...",
